## A streamlined .gitignore for modern .NET projects
## including temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular .NET tools. If you are
## developing with Visual Studio, the VS .gitignore
## https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
## has more thorough IDE-specific entries.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg

# dotenv environment variables file
.env

# Others
~$*
*~
CodeCoverage/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml
nunit-*.xml

# Raw measurement runs contain whole-machine capture health data and are reproducible from
# the seeded workload. Only curated, fixture-scoped evidence is committed (section 13.6).
fixtures/**/runs/

# A diagnostic ETL and an admitted journal hold records from every process on the machine, not only
# the fixture's. Their counters are committed; their records never are (P16). The .ijp0 pattern stays
# for the runs recorded before the capture path moved onto journal-v1.
bench/results/**/*.etl
bench/results/**/*.icatj
bench/results/**/*.ijp0

# A load series writes one truth log per level, and the high levels reach tens of megabytes. The
# series result carries every counter; the per-level oracles stay local and are reproducible.
bench/results/**/levels/**/truth-*.jsonl

# Capture-impact reports keep the aggregate impact.json at the run root. Per-pair source directories
# contain whole-machine journals and reproducible truth logs, so they remain local (P16).
bench/results/capture-impact-*/sources/
.vs/
